WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.250
Drop a strip of a reactive
metal into acid, and it fizzes.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.670
Drop in a carbonate powder,
and that fizzes too.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.250
Now stir in a metal oxide.

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.970
No bubbles at all.

5
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.670
Yet all three reactions make a salt.

6
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.170
And the acid decides the second
half of that salt's name,

7
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.190
every single time.

8
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.410
So why do some reactions of
acids fizz, while others do not?

9
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.970
In this mission, you'll
meet the pH scale,

10
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:30.460
and the ions that make a
solution acidic or alkaline.

11
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.390
You'll find out what
acids make with metals,

12
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.830
with bases and with carbonates,
and how to name the salt.

13
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.250
Your mission: explain why only
some acid reactions fizz.
